; On another thread, exit posts the shutdown to the main thread; what the
; console reads after it never runs. Unload actions run outside any task,
; as for every exit, since a task paused in one would wait on a queue the
; exit has closed.
> (import (place))
> (thread-join (fork-thread (lambda () (exit) (display "never"))))
configuration unloading
unloading outside any task
keeper unloading
> (display "never runs")
